# RST AI Copilot for Prometheus — End User License Agreement

Version 1.1 · Effective 2026-10-06

This End User License Agreement (the "Agreement") is between Anhui Reallysec
Information Technology Ltd. (安徽斯普朗克信息技术有限公司, "Reallysec") and the
individual or entity that installs or uses the Software ("you"). If you accept
this Agreement on behalf of an organization, you represent that you have the
authority to bind that organization, and "you" refers to that organization.

**How you accept.** You accept this Agreement by installing, activating, or
using the Software. In addition, the Software asks each User, when they first
sign in and again whenever the version of this Agreement changes, to confirm
that they have read and agree to it, and a User who does not agree cannot use
the Software. Where the Software has no individual user identity, an
administrator accepts on behalf of the installation. If you do not agree, do
not install or use the Software.

**Please read the sections in bold with particular care. They limit Reallysec's
warranties, indemnity and liability (Sections 9, 10 and 11), restrict how you
may use the Software (Sections 3 and 14), and set out your responsibilities for
Your Data and the destinations you send it to (Section 6), for AI-generated
output, and for changes the Software makes in your Prometheus and Alertmanager
at your direction (Section 9.3).**

## 1. Definitions

- **"Software"** means RST AI Copilot for Prometheus in object-code form as
  delivered by Reallysec, including container images, deployment files,
  compiled feature modules, documentation, content packs, and any updates
  Reallysec provides. The Software is a network-operations assistant that reads
  from the Prometheus, Alertmanager and Grafana systems you connect it to and,
  at your direction, writes alert rules and silences to them.
- **"Documentation"** means the user and installation guides Reallysec publishes
  for the Software at https://reallysec.com/docs/prometheus-ai-copilot.
- **"License"** means the license key or license file issued by Reallysec that
  specifies your edition, feature set, node count, user count, and term.
- **"Edition"** means the Community, Professional, or Enterprise edition, or a
  trial. The Professional and Enterprise editions and trials are stated in your
  License; the Community Edition is the Software used without a License.
- **"Paid Edition"** means the Professional or Enterprise edition under a License
  for which you have paid the applicable fees. A trial is not a Paid Edition.
- **"Subscription Term"** means the term of a Paid Edition License stated in
  your License or Order.
- **"Node"** means one running installation of the Software, identified by its
  installation identifier and host fingerprint.
- **"User"** means an enabled user account in the Software. Disabled and deleted
  accounts are not counted.
- **"Order"** means the quotation, purchase order, or other document under which
  you acquired the License.
- **"Your Data"** means the metrics, alerts, alert rules, silences, device and
  inventory records, configuration, and other data that the Software reads from
  your Prometheus, Alertmanager and Grafana systems or otherwise processes on
  your behalf.
- **"Language-Model Provider"** means the provider of a language-model endpoint
  that you configure in the Software, including a model you host yourself.
- **"AI Output"** means queries, analyses, summaries, answers, proposed alert
  rules, reports, and other content that the Software generates with a
  language model.
- **"Write Actions"** means changes the Software makes in your monitoring
  systems when you or your users instruct it to: writing, changing or removing
  alert rules in the rule files the Software manages and reloading Prometheus
  so they take effect (after approval where the Software requires it), and
  creating or expiring silences in Alertmanager.
- **"Content Pack"** means a file signed by Reallysec that delivers prompts,
  metric dictionaries, rule packs, runbooks and similar content to the Software
  without a new release.

## 2. License Grant

Subject to this Agreement and payment of the applicable fees, Reallysec grants
you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license, for the term
stated in your License, to install and use the Software for your internal
business operations, on no more Nodes and for no more Users than your License
permits, and limited to the features of your Edition. Your employees and
contractors may use the Software on your behalf; you are responsible for their
compliance with this Agreement.

You may run the Software on your own hardware or on infrastructure that you
control and that a cloud or hosting provider operates on your behalf, provided
the provider does not use the Software for its own purposes.

A trial License grants the same rights for evaluation only, for the trial period
stated in the License and for no more than ten (10) Users.

Without a License, Reallysec grants you the same license free of charge and
without a fixed term, limited to the features of the Community Edition, one
User, and one Node. Reallysec may change the features of the Community Edition
in later versions of the Software.

