them under your own agreements with their providers. Reallysec does not control
them and is not responsible for their availability, security, content, or
handling of data you send to them.

## 6. Data and Privacy

### 6.1 Your Data

The Software runs in your environment. Your Data stays under your control, and
you are responsible for it, including under applicable data protection laws.
Reallysec does not receive Your Data through the Software, except during
support access under Section 6.6.

### 6.2 What the Software sends outside your environment

Apart from destinations you configure yourself (such as your Prometheus,
Alertmanager and Grafana, Language-Model Providers, notification channels and
audit-forwarding targets), the Software sends data outside your environment
only as listed here:

- **License service.** When a License is activated online, and afterwards about
  once every twenty-four (24) hours while it remains active (retried about
  every five minutes after a failed attempt), the Software sends Reallysec's
  license service (license.reallysec.com) the license identifier, the product
  identifier and version, a randomly generated installation identifier, the
  host fingerprint (a hash derived from machine identifiers), a timestamp, and
  a random one-time value used to verify the reply. When its license session
  is due for renewal, the Software sends the license identifier, the product
  identifier and version, and the host fingerprint. The license service's
  replies also tell the Software whether the License has been revoked; the
  Software makes no other request for this. Without a License, the Software
  does not contact the license service. Offline activation, where your Edition
  includes it, does not contact the license service.
- **Verification-failure report.** If a downloaded release or Content Pack fails
  signature or checksum verification on an installation with an online-activated
  License, the Software sends the license service the license identifier, the
  product identifier, the version concerned, if known, and the reason for the
  failure.
- **Update checks.** About once a day, and again when an administrator chooses
  to download an update, the Software downloads public release and Content Pack
  files from GitHub Releases, or from a mirror you configure. This applies to
  every Edition, including the Community Edition. These requests send no
  customer data beyond what any HTTP request carries. An installation activated
  offline does not check for updates.
- **Language models.** The Software sends prompts and query results, which may
  include portions of Your Data, to the language-model and embedding endpoints
  you configure, subject to the field masking settings you select, and to no
  other destination. The Software has no built-in endpoint: until you configure
  one, it sends nothing to any Language-Model Provider. Reallysec does not
  receive that data.

The license service also receives the IP address from which each request
comes, as any internet service does. Nothing sent to Reallysec or to GitHub
under this Section includes the contents of your metrics, alerts, alert rules
or queries. Reallysec does not use Your Data to train language models.

### 6.3 How Reallysec uses license-service data

Reallysec uses the data in Section 6.2 that reaches its license service,
including the IP address, only to activate and validate Licenses, to enforce
the Node and User limits of your License, to detect tampered releases and
Content Packs and misuse of Licenses, to verify usage under Section 8, and to
provide support. Reallysec does not sell this data or use it for advertising.
Reallysec keeps it while your License is active and for up to two (2) years
after it ends, or longer only where the law requires, and then deletes or
anonymizes it. Where any of this data is personal information, Reallysec
handles it as described in its privacy notice at https://reallysec.com/privacy-policy.

### 6.4 Language-Model Providers

**Field masking matches known patterns and field names, such as IP addresses,
host names and user names in metric labels. It reduces, but does not guarantee
to remove, personal or sensitive information in what is sent to a
Language-Model Provider. You choose the Language-Model Provider and the masking
settings. You are responsible for your agreement with the Language-Model
Provider, including whether it may retain your data or use it to train models,
and for complying with the laws that apply to sending data to it, including
personal information protection and cross-border data transfer rules.**

### 6.5 Cross-border transfers

**You decide where Your Data goes. If a Language-Model Provider, notification
channel or other destination you configure is outside mainland China, you are
responsible for any security assessment, standard contract, certification,
consent or other requirement that applies to sending data to it.** Reallysec
operates the license service and hosts it in the Hong Kong Special
Administrative Region, outside mainland China, and GitHub
Releases is operated by GitHub outside mainland China. Only the data listed in
Section 6.2 is sent to them. An installation without a License or activated
offline sends nothing to the license service, and an installation activated
offline does not contact GitHub Releases.

### 6.6 Support access

Reallysec accesses your environment or Your Data only when you authorize it in
advance for a specific support request, and only to the extent you authorize.
In doing so Reallysec acts on your behalf as an entrusted party under Article 21
of the Personal Information Protection Law of the People's Republic of China.
Reallysec will process Your Data only to provide the support you requested and
according to your instructions, will keep it confidential, will limit access to
personnel bound by confidentiality obligations, and will not keep copies after
the support is complete unless you agree. On request, Reallysec will sign a
data processing agreement with you that sets out these obligations.

## 7. License Checks, Updates, Support, and Preview Features

**A paid or trial License is checked when it is activated and, for online
activation, at each heartbeat under Section 6.2. If the License expires or is
revoked, the features and User count beyond the Community Edition stop and the
Software continues as the Community Edition. If the online checks of an
online-activated License keep failing beyond the grace period described in the
Documentation, the Software suspends its features, apart from signing in,
license management, settings and viewing the records it already holds, until a
check succeeds again; an administrator can instead deactivate the License and
continue with the Community Edition. Your Data is not deleted.**

Releases and Content Packs are signed by Reallysec, and the Software rejects
any that fail signature or checksum verification. A new release is downloaded
and installed only when an administrator chooses to. By default, a newer
Content Pack found during an update check is applied automatically after it
passes verification. An administrator can turn this off as described in the
Documentation; newer Content Packs are then only stored, and an administrator
chooses whether and when to activate one. An administrator can also return to
an earlier Content Pack.

Reallysec may provide updates during the term of your License, and for the
Community Edition at its discretion. Support, service levels, and maintenance
are provided only as set out in your Order or a separate support agreement.

Features that the Software or the Documentation marks as preview, beta, or
experimental are provided for evaluation. Reallysec may change or remove them
at any time, and Sections 9.1 and 10 do not apply to them.

## 8. Usage Verification

**Self-certification.** At Reallysec's written request, no more than once in
any twelve (12) month period, you will provide within thirty (30) days a
written statement, signed by an authorized representative, of the number of
Nodes on which the Software is installed, the number of Users, and the Edition
in use. Reallysec may also rely on the activation records held by its license
service.

**Audit.** Reallysec, or an independent auditor bound by confidentiality
obligations, may verify your use of the Software no more than once in any
twelve (12) month period, on at least thirty (30) days' written notice, during
your normal business hours, remotely where practicable, and in a way that does
not unreasonably interfere with your business. Information obtained in an audit
is used only to verify compliance with your License and is kept confidential.
Reallysec bears the cost of the audit, unless it shows that you underpaid the
fees due for the audited period by more than five percent (5%), in which case
you will reimburse Reallysec's reasonable audit costs.

If the verification shows use beyond your License, you will pay the applicable
fees for the excess use under Reallysec's then-current price list.

