or agreed in a settlement that Reallysec approves in writing.

**10.2 Procedure.** Reallysec's obligations apply only if you (a) notify
Reallysec in writing promptly enough that its defense is not prejudiced,
(b) give Reallysec sole control of the defense and settlement of the claim, and
(c) provide reasonable cooperation, at Reallysec's expense for your reasonable
out-of-pocket costs. You may take part in the defense with your own counsel at
your own expense. You may not settle the claim without Reallysec's prior written
consent, and Reallysec will not, without your consent, agree to a settlement
that requires you to admit fault or to do anything other than stop using the
Software.

**10.3 Remedies.** If the Software is, or in Reallysec's opinion is likely to
be, held to infringe, Reallysec may at its option and expense (a) obtain the
right for you to continue using it, (b) modify or replace it so that it no
longer infringes without materially reducing its functionality, or (c) if
neither is commercially reasonable, terminate the affected License and refund
the fees you prepaid for the unused remainder of its Subscription Term.

**10.4 Exclusions. Reallysec has no obligation under this Section for any claim
to the extent it arises from: (a) the Community Edition, a trial License or
preview features; (b) modification of the Software by anyone other than
Reallysec; (c) combination of the Software with products, data, or processes
not provided by Reallysec, where the claim would not have arisen without the
combination; (d) AI Output, or the models and services of Language-Model
Providers; (e) third-party and open-source components listed in the
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES file, or the third-party services described in Section 5;
(f) Your Data or other materials you provide; (g) your continued use of the
allegedly infringing Software after Reallysec has told you to stop or has
provided a modification or update that would have avoided the claim; or
(h) your use of the Software in breach of this Agreement.**

**10.5 Limits. Reallysec's obligations under this Section are subject to the
limit in Section 11.2. This Section states Reallysec's entire liability, and
your exclusive remedy, for any claim that the Software infringes or
misappropriates a third party's intellectual property rights.**

